This error is happening because of a tiny but crucial missing keyword: **final**.
You are using Lombok's @RequiredArgsConstructor at the top of your class. This annotation tells Spring Boot to automatically inject dependencies, but **it only works for variables marked as final**.
Because voucherCommandService is missing the final keyword, Spring Boot ignores it, leaves it as null, and your application crashes the moment the scheduler wakes up and tries to use it.
### The Fix
Open your **VoucherExecutionScheduler.java** file and look at the top where your variables are declared (around line 23).
**Change this:**
```java
    private final JdbcTemplate jdbcTemplate;
    private final StringRedisTemplate stringRedisTemplate;
    private VoucherCommandService voucherCommandService;  // <--- Missing 'final'

```
**To this:**
```java
    private final JdbcTemplate jdbcTemplate;
    private final StringRedisTemplate stringRedisTemplate;
    private final VoucherCommandService voucherCommandService; // <--- Added 'final'

```
Once you add the final keyword, restart the application. Spring Boot will correctly inject the service, and your scheduled batches will execute perfectly!
